# Does a real native closure carry Review-owed without a ledger, with that
# debt readable under pipes while push issuance refuses without writes?
# The native CLI dispatch and process streams require this functional route.
#
# The fixture closes its synthetic spec with review-override and explicit
# no-news, then checks the actual commit message and changed paths. A separate
# nonauthorizing debt query names Review-owed and attest. Piped push issuance
# exits 2 with the entire scratch checkout unchanged.

option=timeout:value=60s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture runner/commit-review-owed-trailer
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=review-owed-trailer-written
expect=stdout:contains=review-debt-reported-without-authorization
expect=stdout:contains=push-issuer-refused-without-artifacts
